   "fix": "Either name the functor `restrictScalars` to match `AlgCat.restrictScalars` (and rename the object-level abbrev, e.g. `restrictScalarsObj`), or drop the docstring's 'counterpart' claim and pick an object-level name that does not collide with the Mathlib functor.",
   "issue": "`CommAlgCat.restrictScalars` is the object-level operation (a `K`-algebra viewed as a `k`-algebra), while the functor is `restrictScalarsFunctor`. Mathlib's `AlgCat.restrictScalars` \u2014 which the docstring explicitly calls the analog/counterpart \u2014 is the *functor* `AlgCat S \u2964 AlgCat R` (mathlib/.../AlgCat/Basic.lean:261). A reader carrying the Mathlib name into this parallel namespace expects `CommAlgCat.restrictScalars` to be the functor, not the object map, so the shared name is misleading.",
